\title{Several plans run one after another, each starting once the one before is done}
\description{
The \code{sequence} join of a plan: two to twenty-five plans run one after another.

Each child starts only once the one before it is done, whether it filled or ended, so a sequence is how a plan waits for one order to finish before the next is even considered. A sequence join cannot be a \code{then} join's child, because that child is sized to the first plan's fills.
